00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Let's assume that the transverse leakage

2
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
in one spatial direction can be approximated by a point-wise...

3
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Liquid metal loops coupled to reactors.

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
We can get additional protection with an interlocking screen system.

5
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The reactor coolant pump has a capacity of 90,000 gallons per minute.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Radiation polymerization of ethylene gas...

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The multi-detector position scanner in conjunction with radioactive...

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Our requirements are 10 to the 15th ions per cc temperature of 10 to the 9th degrees Kelvin.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
A reduction of the delayed neutron precursors will make the control problem a little bit...

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Even with the highest worth wrought out, the reactor should be shut down by at least two dollars.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
can be used to create a chimney to stimulate the flow of gas.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
This is the vocabulary of the nuclear age.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
It's a new language or a new way of life.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
A way of life that is rapidly changing under the impact of a growing nuclear industry.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Some of you working in that industry will have a part in the formation of its future.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
It takes time and effort to prepare yourself to work in the fields of nuclear science and engineering.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Since it is your time that's involved, you'll have many questions, such as,

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
How well do these professions pay?

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Will I be making contributions to man's knowledge, to his life?

20
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Can a girl succeed in these fields?

21
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Where do nuclear scientists and engineers live and work?

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
work? This film seeks to answer these questions for those of you who wish to take your place

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:04,000
in the nuclear age. Let's begin by surveying the three main areas in which nuclear scientists

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
and engineers work, primarily laboratories of the U.S. Atomic Energy Commission.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:26,000
colleges and universities, and private nuclear industries.

26
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The Atomic Energy Commission, or AEC, was established by Congress as an independent government agency

27
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
to develop atomic energy for the defense of our country and for peaceful purposes.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:53,000
It is the job of the AEC to control and administer these programs, as well as approving construction and reactor safety standards.

29
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:06,000
In performing its mission, the AEC works through others, sponsoring many different programs and supporting various nuclear facilities.

30
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Educational and research institutions and private industrial firms operate the laboratories.

31
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:21,000
They are always in need of the professional talent required to make the various facilities

32
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
and programs function.

33
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Included in the program areas are the chemical processing of uranium ore, the fabrication

34
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:44,000
of special nuclear products and materials, the design, construction, and operation of

35
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:56,000
reactors, experiments designed to use nuclear energy for space exploration, for the generation

36
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:13,000
of electric power, the desalting of sea water, ship propulsion, preservation of food by irradiation,

37
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
the development of nuclear devices for the peaceful use of nuclear explosives for large

38
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:41,000
excavations, carbon dating various items of antiquity, the application of radioisotopes

39
00:04:41,000 --> 00:05:05,000
to medicine, agriculture, industry, meteorology, crime detection, oceanography, and a host

40
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:12,000
of other activities.

41
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
This national laboratory is only one of the many operated by industrial or university

42
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:24,000
contractors in cooperation with the AEC.

43
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Here nuclear scientists and engineers are involved in both basic and applied research.

44
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:42,000
from America and all parts of the world come here to learn and exchange information.

45
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Our national laboratory facilities are among the finest in the world

46
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
and have an international reputation for accomplishing exciting things

47
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
at the frontiers of nuclear research.

48
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Because creative ideas are so necessary to the development of nuclear energy, there is

49
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:19,000
endless opportunity to use all the know-how and ingenuity you possess.

50
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:24,000
For example, the atom can be used to produce electricity at sea or on land, and it can

51
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:31,000
be used to power space vehicles.

52
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,000
But nuclear scientists and engineers have not yet developed the best reactors for these

53
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:41,000
projects.

54
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:50,000
If you like mysteries and problem solving, then basic nuclear research is your thing.

55
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Then again, if you like to see the end result, applied research might claim your enthusiasm.

56
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
You'll find there are always new ideas to challenge you.

57
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:04,000
For example, you might be involved with the diffusion process, which has become the keystone

58
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:09,000
of the nuclear business.

59
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:15,000
The gaseous diffusion plant is designed to separate fissionable U-235 atoms from the

60
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
more abundant U-238.

61
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:23,000
A steady supply of fissionable uranium is vital to nearly all nuclear activities.

62
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:32,000
It could then be your job to look for new ways to improve the diffusion process.

63
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Or you could have the responsibility of improving plant operations

64
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:53,000
where uranium is cast, rolled, formed, and machined

65
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:59,000
into different shapes for reactive fuels, the most vital ingredient in our nation's nuclear energy program.

66
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:12,000
National laboratories generally have various types of reactors for basic research.

67
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:23,000
This high flux isotope reactor is used to create manmade elements heavier than plutonium.

68
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:35,000
These elements are isotopes which, so far, have not been found in nature.

69
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Using knowledge gained from these isotopes, scientists hope to penetrate such still unexplained

70
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:48,000
phenomena as the formation of stars and the universe.

71
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Basic to the operations of all reactors and the handling of radioactive materials is the

72
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:58,000
monitoring and control of radioactivity. This profession of health physics is a relatively

73
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:04,000
new field requiring a good understanding of the physical, chemical and biological principles

74
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
of radiation.

75
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:20,000
If your interests center on this field, you might be responsible for a plant's radiation

76
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:25,000
protection and training program or doing research on the nature and effects of various types

77
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:39,000
of nuclear radiation.

78
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:44,000
In addition, health physicists contribute to the development of guidelines on radiation

79
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
exposure levels for industry and the general public.

80
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Suppose your interest in basic research was focused on gaining

81
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:02,000
a better understanding of the tremendous forces that bind the atom together.

82
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:14,000
You might use a complex accelerating device such as the cyclotron as a key tool in your research.

83
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:24,000
By shooting high-speed particles approaching the speed of light into selected targets,

84
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:35,000
these devices can change one element into another.

85
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Cyclotrons can produce stable as well as radioactive isotopes.

86
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:47,000
As a staff member of a national laboratory, you might prefer designing and developing

87
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:53,000
experimental equipment for controlling the tremendous energy that is released when hydrogen

88
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:58,000
atoms are forced to combine with one another.

89
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:04,000
This energy, similar to that responsible for the sun's heat and light, is called thermonuclear

90
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:09,000
energy and the process is called nuclear fusion.

91
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
release of this energy has great implications for all mankind since the

92
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:19,000
supply of all other existing fuels including uranium is limited. Once

93
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:24,000
harnessed the energy available from the hydrogen and sea water is estimated as

94
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:34,000
being enough to supply the world's power needs for untold centuries. Among the

95
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
many significant contributions of nuclear science and engineering are the

96
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:46,000
fascinating substances called radioisotopes.

97
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:50,000
These are extremely valuable to researchers in many scientific disciplines when used as

98
00:11:50,000 --> 00:12:01,000
sources of radiation or as tracers.

99
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Most AEC laboratories have a biomedical research program directed, for one thing, toward understanding

100
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:20,000
the changes that occur when living tissues are exposed to radiation.

101
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Such experiments have contributed valuable information to the field of radiation genetics.

102
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Living cells, organs, and organisms are carefully analyzed in the hope of learning more about

103
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:40,000
of the fundamental life processes, including the diagnosis, prevention, and treatment

104
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:44,000
of the many malfunctions and diseases which continue to afflict mankind.

105
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Many complex problems arise in nuclear research

106
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
and development, requiring numerous calculations

107
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,000
and the creation of mathematical models to test a new concept or idea.

108
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:15,000
High speed computers and data processors are handy tools in solving these problems.

109
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Constant progress is being made in nuclear science and engineering, which makes it imperative

110
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,000
for those in the field to keep up with advancements.

111
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:34,000
For this reason, all scientific installations collect and catalog published materials related

112
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,000
to the many fields.

113
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:42,000
In this way, staff members can keep abreast of the progress made in any field which interests

114
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:48,000
them.

115
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Wherever you work as a nuclear scientist or engineer, you'll be encouraged to write reports

116
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,000
about your research for scientific journals and other publications which are generally

117
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:04,000
distributed worldwide.

118
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Informative seminars are held to help keep the staff up to date on the latest developments.

119
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Staff members may attend national and international meetings.

120
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
These usually attract specialists from all over the world.

121
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
As a nuclear scientist or engineer, you'll find that except for information which affects

122
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:38,000
their nation's security, there's a free exchange of knowledge.

123
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:43,000
In private industry, there are unlimited opportunities for nuclear scientists and engineers.

124
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Many such companies have extensive research and development programs, as well as production

125
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:54,000
activities.

126
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:58,000
This installation is an example of a firm whose staff is engaged in applying the energy

127
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:11,000
of the atom to a wide variety of peaceful uses.

128
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:16,000
In a company such as this, you could be involved in the design, development, and the improvement

129
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:20,000
power reactors manufactured by the company to generate electricity for

130
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:24,000
public consumption. The business of producing mass quantities of electricity

131
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:29,000
by means of the atom is relatively new.

132
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Companies engaged in the manufacture of nuclear power plants and their customers

133
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:45,000
the electric utilities are constantly searching for ways to increase the

134
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:52,000
capacity and efficiency of their products.

135
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:57,000
The purpose is to provide the power required by our ever-expanding population and industry

136
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:05,000
at the lowest possible cost.

137
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:10,000
This means the development of new concepts in reactor design and construction, as well

138
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:18,000
as improved materials.

139
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:23,000
As a nuclear engineer employed by private industry, your responsibility could involve

140
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:37,000
the designing of nuclear instrumentation for research, production, and training purposes.

141
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Some firms are engaged in controlled fusion research in the belief that the energy released

142
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:48,000
from this type of nuclear reaction will ultimately replace coal and oil and even nuclear fission

143
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:57,000
as man's main source of energy.

144
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Experiments here are concerned with containing the plasma formed from deuterium, an isotope

145
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:09,000
of hydrogen at super high temperatures so that the deuterium nuclei will unite or fuse.

146
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:14,000
In fusion, enormous amounts of energy are released which could be used to produce electric

147
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:19,000
power.

148
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Not all nuclear scientists or engineers are interested in research and development.

149
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:28,000
There are those who derive more personal satisfaction from working on the production or construction

150
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:38,000
side of a private nuclear industry's activities.

151
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,000
If you're this type of person, you could be employed in developing and improving a company's

152
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:51,000
fuel production program or involved in the fabrication of other reactor components.

153
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:55,000
On the other hand, you might be a part of a company team, which supervises the installation

154
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:59,000
and initial operation of the power and research reactors it manufactures.

155
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,000
This type of work will take you to many parts of the United States

156
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
and to many countries around the world.

157
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:16,000
AEC Laboratories and Private Industry will offer you ample opportunity

158
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
to advance your knowledge and proficiency.

159
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Courses may be given by various universities at AEC installations

160
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
to help you earn credits toward an advanced degree.

161
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Otherwise, you can continue your education in a nearby college or university.

162
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:38,000
In many instances, your employer will assume all or most of the tuition costs.

163
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Wherever you work, it will be to your benefit to further your education

164
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:52,000
because as your proficiency increases, so will your opportunities for job and financial advancement.

165
00:18:53,000 --> 00:19:03,000
With the growing demand for nuclear scientists and engineers has come an increasing need

166
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:07,000
for teachers in these fields.

167
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:11,000
Should you become attracted to campus life, your association with faculty members in your

168
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:20,000
own or other fields can be a daily rewarding stimulation.

169
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Teaching offers many rewards, but perhaps the greatest is the satisfaction that comes

170
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:34,000
from your ability to communicate what you know to others.

171
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Teaching is deeply involved in the shaping of the characters, the ambitions, and the

172
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:45,000
goals of those who come to learn.

173
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:52,000
At the college and university level, research is an integral part of teaching.

174
00:19:52,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Many significant discoveries are made where faculty members combine instruction with research.

175
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Teaching allows considerably more freedom than is found in most professions.

176
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Opportunities often exist for professors to pursue their research at a national laboratory

177
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
or at another university.

178
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Many universities also have agreements with foreign universities, whereby faculty members are

179
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
exchanged on an annual basis.

180
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Most universities also provide professors with sabbatical leaves, which can be a year off

181
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
with partial or full salary.

182
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:47,000
during which time they may pursue new studies or conduct scientific investigations at other

183
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:56,000
research centers.

184
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Many professors supplement their income by serving as consultants to industrial concerns

185
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,000
and research organizations.

186
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:12,000
write newspaper and magazine articles, textbooks, novels, science fiction stories and the like.

187
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:22,000
Some appear on radio and television as science commentators or instructors.

188
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:29,000
But by far the greatest reward for those who teach springs from the deep feeling of personal

189
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
satisfaction that the work they are doing is contributing to the overall well-being

190
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:46,000
and progress of their fellow man.

191
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Working as a nuclear scientist or engineer, you'll find your living, as a rule, better

192
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:55,000
than average.

193
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Most areas offer modern, spacious homes and excellent schools.

194
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:08,000
find in your community cultural and recreational activities to satisfy practically every taste and

195
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:26,000
interest and if you're someone who likes to devote your leisure time to the great outdoors

196
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:30,000
you'll have almost unlimited opportunities anywhere you happen to be employed

197
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:41,000
It's, of course, impossible to show you every area in which nuclear scientists and engineers

198
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:47,000
are presently playing and will go on playing a vital role in man's progress to a better

199
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:52,000
life.

200
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Research institutions, national and international organizations, such federal government agencies

201
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:02,000
as the AEC, NASA, the Department of Defense, and many others

202
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:08,000
will need more and more nuclear specialists as the nuclear fields continue to grow and expand.

203
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:24,000
And there's no question, women can and do succeed in these professions.

204
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Many companies, colleges, and universities, research institutions, and government agencies

205
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:47,000
already have women on their staffs, and more would be employed if more were available and

206
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:50,000
qualified.

207
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:55,000
scientists and engineers find their work professionally and personally stimulating.

208
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:11,000
If you have the interest, the capabilities, and the required training, you can join in the high

209
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:17,000
adventure, the sense of achievement, and the many rewards that accrue to those exploring the

210
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:23,000
fascinating world of the atom. All you need to do is decide to take your place in the nuclear age.
